-- Precedence between instruments (MMS-521), and the interface every root
-- implements. Each collection of instruments has a root that is a
-- `collection root`: the instruments it includes, what each says for a case,
-- and the collection's own ruling, by the collection's own rule (the client,
-- 2026-10-22: "each root should be an interface, agreement precedence is
-- the agreement root's responsibility"):
--   - among collective agreements, the provision in the employee's favour
--     (the Collective Agreements Law, §23): l4/lib/agreements-root.l4;
--   - among circulars to the owners, the later replaces the earlier on the
--     same point (convention precedence.later-circular):
--     l4/lib/circulars-root.l4;
--   - the takanon speaks once on an item: l4/lib/takanon-root.l4.
-- The root (l4/lib/root.l4) asks every collection for its ruling and settles
-- between them here, by the rules that are the instruments' own and the
-- law's; none is invented here:
--   1. The takanon's introduction (takanon/terms-service.education.gov.il/
--      terms.l4, `prevails over the takanon`): where the takanon does not
--      match a collective agreement, the law, a Director-General's circular,
--      a Ministry procedure or a more recent circular to the owners, they
--      prevail. If any instrument that prevails over it speaks, the takanon
--      is out; if none does, the takanon governs over the rest.
--   2. Between an agreement and the term the employer pays by (a circular's
--      figure), the term stands where it is in the employee's favour and the
--      agreement does not forbid it (§22; convention
--      instruments.favourable-circular) — but first, for a budgeted or
--      supported employer, what goes beyond the agreement stands only as far
--      as the Budget Foundations Law §29 permits (convention
--      instruments.section-29-approval). A lower term yields to the agreement:
--      "a circular never out-ranks an agreement" (precedence.agreement).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT collective_agreements_law
IMPORT budget_foundations_law

§ `סדר העדיפות בין המסמכים — מקום אחד לכל הכללים`

§§ `שמות הכללים`

-- The rules a ruling names, each once: a resolution in the root cites the
-- same name, so it cannot drift from what precedence applies.
`§22: a term in the employee's favour stands` MEANS "חוק הסכמים קיבוציים, סעיף 22: תנאי לטובת העובד עומד"
`§29: the excess over the agreement is void` MEANS "חוק יסודות התקציב, סעיף 29: העודף על ההסכם בטל"
`a circular never out-ranks the agreement` MEANS "חוזר אינו גובר על ההסכם שהוא מבצע"
`the only instrument that speaks` MEANS "המסמך היחיד שמדבר"
`the takanon's introduction: nothing that prevails over it speaks` MEANS "מבוא התקנון: אף מסמך שגובר על התקנון אינו מדבר"
`the takanon's introduction: a more recent circular prevails` MEANS "מבוא התקנון: חוזר מאוחר יותר גובר"
`a later circular replaces an earlier one` MEANS "חוזר מאוחר גובר על חוזר מוקדם בעניין אחד"
`§23: the provision in the employee's favour` MEANS "חוק הסכמים קיבוציים, סעיף 23: ההוראה שלטובת העובד"
`the takanon's introduction: an agreement prevails` MEANS "מבוא התקנון: הסכם קיבוצי גובר על התקנון"
`no instrument speaks` MEANS "אין מסמך"

§§ `מסמך וטענתו`

@desc What one instrument says a pay item is, for one case.
DECLARE `claim` HAS
    `by`     IS AN `instrument`
    `answer` IS A NUMBER

@desc Which instrument governs a pay item for a case, what it gives, and by which rule.
DECLARE `ruling` HAS
    `the answer`  IS A NUMBER
    `governed by` IS AN `instrument`
    `by the rule` IS A STRING

GIVEN i IS AN `instrument`, a IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `claim`
DECIDE `the claim of` i a IS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST n THEN JUST (`claim` WITH `by` IS i, `answer` IS n)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `ממשק השורשים`

-- The interface every root implements: a collection of instruments, what
-- each says for a case, and the collection's own ruling. The root holds a
-- list of them and settles between their rulings (below).
@desc A root of a collection of instruments: what it includes, what each says, and how the collection itself decides.
DECLARE `collection root` HAS
    `the collection`  IS A STRING @desc its name, in Hebrew
    `its instruments` IS A LIST OF `instrument`
    `what each says`  IS A FUNCTION FROM `pay item` AND `teaching case` TO LIST OF `claim`
    `its ruling`      IS A FUNCTION FROM `pay item` AND `teaching case` TO MAYBE `ruling`

-- A function kept in a record is called through a rule that takes it as an
-- input (the parser reads `(r's f) x` as no call at all).
GIVEN f IS A FUNCTION FROM `pay item` AND `teaching case` TO LIST OF `claim`
      i IS A `pay item`
      c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `the claims f gives` f i c IS f i c

GIVEN f IS A FUNCTION FROM `pay item` AND `teaching case` TO MAYBE `ruling`
      i IS A `pay item`
      c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling f gives` f i c IS f i c

GIVEN r IS A `collection root`, i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `what the collection's instruments say` r i c IS
    `the claims f gives` (r's `what each says`) i c

GIVEN r IS A `collection root`, i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ruling`
DECIDE `the collection's ruling` r i c IS
    `the ruling f gives` (r's `its ruling`) i c

-- The claim a ruling makes for its collection, set against another
-- collection's.
GIVEN r IS A `ruling`
GIVETH A `claim`
DECIDE `the claim of the ruling` r IS
    `claim` WITH `by` IS r's `governed by`, `answer` IS r's `the answer`

GIVEN r IS A `ruling`, rule IS A STRING
GIVETH A `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling by the rule` r rule IS
    `ruling` WITH `the answer` IS r's `the answer`, `governed by` IS r's `governed by`, `by the rule` IS rule

§§ `1 מבוא התקנון`

GIVEN r IS A `ruling`, `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ruling prevails over the takanon` r `the takanon's provision was last amended` IF
    `prevails over the takanon`
        (`conflicting source` WITH
            `source kind`   IS r's `governed by`'s `kind`
            `source issued` IS r's `governed by`'s `issued`)
        `the takanon's provision was last amended`

GIVEN rulings IS A LIST OF `ruling`
GIVETH A LIST OF `ruling`
DECIDE `the takanon's rulings` rulings IS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `governed by`'s `is the takanon`) rulings

GIVEN rulings IS A LIST OF `ruling`
GIVETH A LIST OF `ruling`
DECIDE `the other collections' rulings` rulings IS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD NOT r's `governed by`'s `is the takanon`) rulings

-- The takanon stands where it speaks and nothing that prevails over it
-- does. Another collection's ruling is its strongest instrument — the most
-- favourable agreement, the latest circular — so if any of its instruments
-- prevails over the takanon, its ruling does.
GIVEN rulings IS A LIST OF `ruling`
      `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the takanon stands` rulings `the takanon's provision was last amended` IF
        NOT null (`the takanon's rulings` rulings)
    AND NOT any (GIVEN r YIELD `the ruling prevails over the takanon` r `the takanon's provision was last amended`)
                (`the other collections' rulings` rulings)

§§ `2 הסכם מול התנאי שהמעסיק משלם לפיו — סעיפים 22 ו־29`

-- The employer, as the Budget Foundations Law tells bodies apart: an
-- owner other than a local authority is taken as a body declared
-- supported, the strictest case (as circular תש"ע/2 does).
GIVEN e IS A `the teacher's employer`
GIVETH AN `employing body`
DECIDE `the body section 29 asks about` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `employed by the State` THEN `the State as an employing body`
    WHEN `employed by a local authority` THEN `a local authority`
    WHEN `employed by another owning body` THEN `a body declared supported`

-- §29 first: the employer's term, cut back to the agreement's amount where
-- the employer is bound by §29 and the term is neither as practised for all
-- state employees nor approved. Then §22 between the agreement and what
-- stands.
GIVEN agreement IS A `claim`, term IS A `claim`, e IS A `the teacher's employer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what the employer's term gives under section 29` agreement term e IS
    `the amount that stands under section 29`
        (term's `answer`)
        (agreement's `answer`)
        (`section 29 permits the change`
            (`the body section 29 asks about` e)
            (term's `by`'s `practised for all state employees`)
            (term's `by`'s `approved by the Finance Minister`)
            FALSE)

GIVEN agreement IS A `claim`, term IS A `claim`, e IS A `the teacher's employer`
GIVETH A `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling between an agreement and the employer's term` agreement term e IS
    IF      `the amount that governs between agreement and contract` (agreement's `answer`) `what stands` FALSE EQUALS `what stands`
        AND `what stands` GREATER THAN agreement's `answer`
    THEN `ruling` WITH
             `the answer`  IS `what stands`
             `governed by` IS term's `by`
             `by the rule` IS `§22: a term in the employee's favour stands`
    ELSE `ruling` WITH
             `the answer`  IS agreement's `answer`
             `governed by` IS agreement's `by`
             `by the rule` IS (IF term's `answer` GREATER THAN agreement's `answer`
                               THEN `§29: the excess over the agreement is void`
                               ELSE `a circular never out-ranks the agreement`)
    WHERE
        `what stands` MEANS `what the employer's term gives under section 29` agreement term e

§§ `ההכרעה בין האוספים`

GIVEN c IS A `claim`, rule IS A STRING
GIVETH A `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling for` c rule IS
    `ruling` WITH `the answer` IS c's `answer`, `governed by` IS c's `by`, `by the rule` IS rule

-- The one ruling for a pay item and a case, from each collection's own
-- ruling: the employer, and the date the takanon's provision on the item was
-- last amended. NOTHING where no collection speaks.
GIVEN rulings IS A LIST OF `ruling`
      e IS A `the teacher's employer`
      `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling between the collections` rulings e `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS
    IF `the takanon stands` rulings `the takanon's provision was last amended`
    THEN CONSIDER `the takanon's rulings` rulings
         WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
         WHEN t FOLLOWED BY ts THEN
             JUST (`the ruling by the rule` t
                       (IF null (`the other collections' rulings` rulings)
                        THEN `the only instrument that speaks`
                        ELSE `the takanon's introduction: nothing that prevails over it speaks`))
    ELSE `the ruling between agreement and employer`
             (`the other collections' rulings` rulings) e
             (NOT null (`the takanon's rulings` rulings))

-- What is left once the takanon is out (or never spoke): the agreements'
-- ruling, the employer's term (the circulars' ruling), or the two settled by
-- §§22 and 29. A collection's own rule stands, save that where the takanon
-- spoke and is out, its one instrument governs by the takanon's introduction.
GIVEN left IS A LIST OF `ruling`
      e IS A `the teacher's employer`
      `the takanon is out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling between agreement and employer` left e `the takanon is out` IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `governed by`'s `kind` EQUALS `a collective agreement`) left
    WHEN EMPTY THEN
        CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD NOT r's `governed by`'s `kind` EQUALS `a collective agreement`) left
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
        WHEN t FOLLOWED BY ts THEN
            JUST (`the ruling by the rule` t
                      (IF `the takanon is out` AND t's `by the rule` EQUALS `the only instrument that speaks`
                       THEN `the takanon's introduction: a more recent circular prevails`
                       ELSE t's `by the rule`))
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY more THEN
        CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD NOT r's `governed by`'s `kind` EQUALS `a collective agreement`) left
        WHEN EMPTY THEN
            JUST (`the ruling by the rule` a
                      (IF `the takanon is out` AND a's `by the rule` EQUALS `the only instrument that speaks`
                       THEN `the takanon's introduction: an agreement prevails`
                       ELSE a's `by the rule`))
        WHEN t FOLLOWED BY ts THEN
            JUST (`the ruling between an agreement and the employer's term`
                      (`the claim of the ruling` a) (`the claim of the ruling` t) e)

`no instrument` MEANS
    `instrument` WITH
        `module`        IS ""
        `title`         IS ""
        `kind`          IS `another source`
        `is the takanon` IS FALSE
        `issued`        IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1900
        `practised for all state employees` IS FALSE
        `approved by the Finance Minister`  IS FALSE
